<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mallorca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Majorca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mallorca, or Majorca, is the largest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palma">Palma</a>. Home to the Talaiotic culture in prehistory, it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 123 BCE and ruled by Muslim dynasties from 902, including the Banu Ghaniya. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> conquered it in 1229 and made it the centre of the Kingdom of Majorca, and it now forms part of the Spanish autonomous community of the Balearic Islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mallorca.jpg" alt="Mallorca" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mallorca.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
